{"name":"Longan’s Kernel","hex":"#442117","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"longan","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen tree, Dimocarpus longan, of the Sapindaceae family, native to southern China.","The fruit from the longan tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/longan"},{"term":"kernel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The core, center, or essence of an object or system.","The central (usually edible) part of a nut, especially once the hard shell has been removed."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To enclose within a kernel","To crenellate"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kernel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Longan","blocks":[{"text":"Longan, also called lungan or dragon's eye, is a tropical tree species that produces edible fruit. It is one of the better-known tropical members of the soapberry family Sapindaceae, to which the lychee and rambutan also belong. The fruit of the longan is similar to lychee, but has a milder, and more subtle aroma and sweetness. The species is native to Southeast Asia and southern China. Today, China, Thailand, and Vietnam are the largest producers of longan fruit, together accounting for approximately 95% of global production."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Longan_tree_at_Pine_Island_Nursery.jpg/330px-Longan_tree_at_Pine_Island_Nursery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Longan","wikidata":"Q193449"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Longan_%28Dimocarpus_longan%29_Tree_lower_trunk.jpg/330px-Longan_%28Dimocarpus_longan%29_Tree_lower_trunk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Longan_%28Dimocarpus_longan%29_Tree_lower_trunk.jpg/960px-Longan_%28Dimocarpus_longan%29_Tree_lower_trunk.jpg?utm_source=en